# Enforcement points
1. ContentView.startImport(choices)  — UI funnel for every entry point (picker, drop, Shortcut, open-with, Add Files):
   measures the files (folders recursively, symlinks ignored), reads the archive's ingested bytes from the sources
   table, refuses the whole import if the total would pass 100 MB, shows the "Import refused" alert and raises a
   purchase request on Personal with the figures.
2. ContentViewModel.parseSelectedFiles(..., inputByteLimit:) — service boundary, same check, so no caller that skips
   the funnel can ingest past the limit; a refused run imports nothing and reports the reason in the status line and
   the import queue.
3. GuidedImportSheet — "Free plan input allowance" section ahead of the Start button (allowance, already imported,
   this import adds, after this import); Start disabled while measuring or when over; "Unlock with Personal…".
   Paid tiers: no section, no limit.

